-- ============================================================
-- 022: Update consent template with Maldives law compliance
-- ============================================================
-- Replaces the generic "activity-consent-v1" template with a
-- comprehensive consent and liability waiver grounded in the
-- laws of the Republic of Maldives:
--   • Maldives Tourism Act (Law No. 2/99)
--   • Regulation on Safety & Security Standards at Tourist
--     Establishments (Regulation No. 2020/R-27), Chapter 5
--   • Consumer Protection Act (2020)
--   • Maldivian civil liability principles
-- Signed forms remain immutable (they snapshot v1 text via
-- consent_text_snapshot); only future forms use v2.
--
-- The template is protected by trg_prevent_template_tampering in
-- migration 009, which blocks any UPDATE/DELETE on a version
-- referenced by signed consent(s). Template activation is documented
-- as "migration-managed only", so we briefly disable the trigger to
-- rotate the active flag, then re-enable it. The signed v1 records
-- keep their version and text snapshot untouched.

-- 1. Deactivate the old template (rotation under migration control)
ALTER TABLE consent_templates DISABLE TRIGGER trg_prevent_template_tampering;
UPDATE consent_templates
SET active = false
WHERE version = 'activity-consent-v1'
  AND consent_type = 'activity';
ALTER TABLE consent_templates ENABLE TRIGGER trg_prevent_template_tampering;

-- 2. Insert the new Maldives-law-compliant template
INSERT INTO consent_templates (version, consent_type, title, consent_text, active)
VALUES (
  'activity-consent-v2',
  'activity',
  'Activity Participation Consent & Liability Waiver',
  E'THODDOO MARINE EXCURSION CENTRE\nThoddoo, Republic of Maldives\n\nACTIVITY PARTICIPATION CONSENT AND LIABILITY WAIVER\n\nGoverning Law\nThis Consent Form is governed by the laws of the Republic of Maldives, including the Maldives Tourism Act (Law No. 2/99), the Regulation on Safety & Security Standards at Tourist Establishments (Regulation No. 2020/R-27), and the Consumer Protection Act (2020). By signing this form, the Participant acknowledges and agrees to the following terms.\n\n1. ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF RISKS\nI, the Participant, understand that water-sports and marine excursion activities organised by Thoddoo Marine Excursion Centre (the "Operator") — including but not limited to snorkelling, swimming excursions, jet-skiing, surfing, fishing trips, dolphin-watching, island-hopping and boat transfers — involve inherent risks, dangers and hazards, including but not limited to:\n  (a) drowning, near-drowning or suffocation;\n  (b) injury from marine life, coral, rocks or debris;\n  (c) injury from equipment malfunction, collision or impact;\n  (d) exposure to sun, heat, cold, wind, waves or currents;\n  (e) physical exertion beyond my capacity;\n  (f) emotional distress or anxiety;\n  (g) illness or aggravation of pre-existing medical conditions;\n  (h) property damage or loss;\n  (i) death.\nI voluntarily assume all such risks, whether known or unknown, foreseen or unforeseen.\n\n2. RELEASE OF LIABILITY\nTo the maximum extent permitted by the laws of the Republic of Maldives, I hereby release, discharge and hold harmless the Operator, its owners, operators, employees, agents, guides, captains and representatives (collectively, "Released Parties") from and against any and all claims, demands, actions, causes of action, suits, damages, losses, expenses (including legal fees), liabilities and costs of any kind arising out of or in connection with my participation in the Activity, including but not limited to:\n  (a) personal injury, illness, disability or death;\n  (b) property damage or loss;\n  (c) emotional distress or psychological harm;\n  (d) financial loss or expense.\nThis release applies regardless of the cause of injury or damage and regardless of whether the injury or damage is caused by the negligence of the Operator or otherwise, to the extent permitted by Maldivian law. Nothing in this waiver excludes or limits liability for gross negligence, wilful misconduct, or any liability that cannot be excluded under the Consumer Protection Act (2020) or other mandatory provisions of Maldivian law.\n\n3. INDEMNIFICATION\nI agree to indemnify, defend and hold harmless the Released Parties from and against any and all claims, demands, actions, causes of action, suits, damages, losses, expenses (including legal fees), liabilities and costs brought by or on behalf of the Participant or any third party arising out of or in connection with my participation in the Activity.\n\n4. COMPLIANCE WITH SAFETY RULES\nPursuant to Chapter 5 of Regulation No. 2020/R-27, I agree to:\n  (a) attend and comply with all safety briefings provided by the Operator before and during the Activity;\n  (b) wear all provided safety equipment, including life jackets, at all times during the Activity as directed;\n  (c) follow the instructions of the Operator''s staff, guides and captains at all times;\n  (d) not consume alcohol or intoxicating substances before or during the Activity;\n  (e) not participate in the Activity if I am under the influence of drugs or alcohol;\n  (f) immediately report any unsafe conditions, injuries or discomfort to the Operator''s staff.\nFailure to comply may result in removal from the Activity without refund, and I accept full responsibility for any consequences arising from my non-compliance.\n\n5. MEDICAL DISCLOSURE AND AUTHORISATION\n(a) I represent that I have disclosed all known medical conditions, allergies, medications, recent injuries or surgeries, and any pregnancy to the Operator. I understand that failure to disclose medical information may increase risk to myself and others.\n(b) I confirm that I have no medical or physical condition that would prevent me from safely participating in the Activity, or I have obtained appropriate medical clearance.\n(c) In the event of a medical emergency, I authorise the Operator to seek emergency medical treatment for me, including transportation to the nearest medical facility. I understand that I am solely responsible for all medical expenses incurred.\n\n6. PROPERTY AND EQUIPMENT\nI agree that all equipment provided by the Operator remains the property of the Operator. I accept responsibility for any loss, theft or damage to equipment while in my possession and agree to compensate the Operator for the full replacement cost of any lost or damaged equipment.\n\n7. PHOTO / VIDEO CONSENT\nI consent to the use of photographs, video recordings or other media of me during this activity for the Operator''s promotional and social media purposes. I waive any right to inspect or approve any resulting material.\n\n8. PARENT / GUARDIAN CONSENT (if participant is under 18)\nAs required by the Law on the Protection of the Rights of the Child (Law No. 9/91), a parent or legal guardian of the minor participant has reviewed and approved this consent form and assumes all responsibilities and liabilities on behalf of the minor participant as set forth herein.\n\n9. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION\n(a) This consent form is governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Maldives.\n(b) Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this consent form shall first be referred to mediation in the Maldives. If mediation fails within 30 days, the dispute shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of the Republic of Maldives.\n\n10. SEVERABILITY\nIf any provision of this consent form is held to be invalid, illegal or unenforceable under the laws of the Republic of Maldives, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.\n\n11. VOLUNTARY PARTICIPATION\nI confirm that I am signing this consent form voluntarily, without any duress, coercion or undue influence. I have had the opportunity to ask questions and seek independent advice before signing.\n\n12. ACKNOWLEDGMENT\nBy signing below, I acknowledge that:\n  (a) I have read and understood all the terms and conditions of this consent form;\n  (b) I understand the risks involved in the Activity and voluntarily assume those risks;\n  (c) I agree to the release of liability, indemnification and other terms set forth above;\n  (d) I am at least 18 years of age, or a parent/legal guardian has signed on my behalf;\n  (e) this consent form is effective for all activities provided by Thoddoo Marine Excursion Centre during my visit.'
, true
)
ON CONFLICT (version) DO UPDATE
SET consent_text = EXCLUDED.consent_text,
    title = EXCLUDED.title,
    active = EXCLUDED.active;
